{
  "reasoning": "The defendants were village officials who abused their positions to manipulate public land and social insurance resources for personal gain. They collected large sums of cash from relatives by falsely claiming fees for processing loss-of-land farmer pension insurance, and they allocated public land to individuals to qualify for insurance benefits, effectively defrauding the state and the victims. This conduct constitutes fraud (诈骗) for deceiving the victims and misappropriating funds, and also a breach of fiduciary duty by misusing public assets, which fits the crime of embezzlement/occupation of public assets (职务侵占). No evidence of other crimes such as bribery or drug offenses is present. Therefore the appropriate charges are 诈骗 and 职务侵占.",
  "final_answer": "[罪名]诈骗;职务侵占<eoa>"
}
